# Shared agent memory

This project keeps portable shared memory in `.agent-memory/`. Markdown is the
source of truth; the SQLite FTS5 index is a disposable cache. Any coding agent
(Codex, Cursor, OpenCode, Antigravity, DeepSeek Harness, ...) reads and writes
the same files.

## Before work

1. Read `.agent-memory/INDEX.md` and `.agent-memory/task_on_progress.md`.
2. Read `.agent-memory/HISTORY.md` when the task touches architecture or major behavior.
3. Search memory: `agent-memory search "<keywords>"`. If the CLI is unavailable,
   fall back to `rg -n -i "<keywords>" .agent-memory/`.
4. Read only the top few relevant files. Do not load the whole folder.

## During work

- Keep `.agent-memory/task_on_progress.md` current.
- Record important discoveries, constraints, failed approaches and decisions.
- Never store secrets; redact with `<REDACTED>` or `<ENV_VAR_NAME>`.

## After work

1. Update `.agent-memory/task_on_progress.md`.
2. Append major changes to `.agent-memory/HISTORY.md`.
3. Write a session note when useful: `agent-memory new session "<title>"`.
4. Promote memories that change future behavior: `agent-memory promote <id> <type>`.
5. Rebuild the index: `agent-memory rebuild`.

